{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-dilog-heat-partition","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-dilog-heat-partition","kind":"remark","title":"$\\mathrm{Li}_2^q$ as the $q$-heat partition function","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-dilogarithm","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-laplace","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-kernel-peter-weyl"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-dilogarithm","tags":["hopf-algebra","dilogarithm","q-heat","partition-function"],"text":"q-dilog-heat-partition.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-dilog-heat-partition\"></a><p>The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-dilogarithm generates the partition function of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat flow. The contour integral of the resolvent against the spectrum sums logarithmic branches at each eigenvalue <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda_j(q)</code> to produce <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_2^q</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-dilog-heat-partition.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.24.7","page":"b/rem-q-dilog-heat-partition","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":0,"warn":2,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
